Debian Packaging for Helm
==========================

This package follows the DEP-14 Git repository layout for Debian packages.

Repository Layout
-----------------

This repository follows DEP-14 (Debian Enhancement Proposal 14) for Git
packaging repository layout:

Branch Naming:
- debian/master or debian/sid: Main development branch
- debian/<release>: Stable release branches (e.g., debian/bookworm)
- upstream: Upstream source branch (if used)
- pristine-tar: Pristine-tar delta files (if used)

Tag Naming:
- debian/<version>: Debian package release tags
- upstream/<version>: Upstream release tags

Upstream Source
---------------

The upstream source for Helm is available at:
  https://github.com/helm/helm

The package tracks the latest stable releases from the upstream repository.

Building the Package
--------------------

To build this package, you need the following dependencies:
- debhelper (>= 13)
- dh-golang
- golang (>= 1.19)

Build the package using:
  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc

Or using sbuild/pbuilder for a clean build environment.

Standards Compliance
--------------------

This package aims to comply with:
- Debian Policy Manual (version 4.6.2 or later)
- DEP-14 for Git repository layout
- Go packaging guidelines for Debian

